      <div type="clause" n="44.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 44.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="xno" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="517" ed="#liebermann"/>E se cil i defa[l]t<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#LeisWl_44-2.lnote.oe.18"/>, de ki il se claime, dunt prenge congé, que<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#LeisWl_44-2.lnote.oe.9"/> il pusse nam prendre pur le son lu[in<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#LeisWl_44-2.lnote.oe.19"/>] e pref.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-l"><pb n="517" ed="#liebermann"/>Quodsi nec tunc ei satisfactum fuerit, accipiat licentiam namium<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#LeisWl_44-2.lnote.oe.2"/> capiendi pro suo et prope et longe.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="44.2" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="272" ed="#robertson"/>E se cil i defa[l]t de ki il se claime, dunt prenge congé que il pusse nam prendre pur le son lu[in] e pref.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="517" ed="#liebermann"/>44, 2. Wenn da aber jener<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#LeisWl_44-2.lnote.de.1"/>, über den er sich beklagt, sich [der Rechtspflicht] entzieht, dann nehme er Erlaubniss, dass er [jenem] Zwangspfand für das [eingeklagte] Seinige fortnehmen dürfe fern<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="f" target="#LeisWl_44-2.lnote.de1.f"/> und nah.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">44, 2. But if there the man of whom he complains withdraws himself [from his legal duty], then he shall take permission that he may take away from [that man] a distress for his own [property sued for], far and near.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="273" ed="#robertson"/>And if the man against whom he is bringing his charge fails to appear, he shall get leave to make distraint for what is his own both far and near.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="517"><ref target="clause:IICn_19-2">II Cn 19.2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 19, 2</note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 272–273 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text and German translation added from Gesetze I p. 517, October 2026 (two independent readings of the page images)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_44-2.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">517</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">qui <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">qui Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_44-2.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">517</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">defait <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">defait I</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_44-2.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">517</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">lum <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lum I</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_44-2.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">517</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">namū, <hi rend="italic">in anderer Tinte Strich über</hi> a <hi rend="italic">S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">namū, stroke over a in different ink S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="LeisWl_44-2.lnote.de1.f" n="f" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">517</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">überall, wo Beklagter Fahrhabe besitzt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">wherever the defendant has chattels</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_44-2.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">292</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘er hier keinen Erfolg hat’, ohne <hi rend="italic">cil, de ki il se claime</hi> zu übersetzen, Schmid falsch</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Schmid’s ‘he has no success here’, which leaves <hi rend="italic">cil, de ki il se claime</hi> untranslated, is wrong</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
